[VoxrCommandParser] Intent 'fire' has the pattern "fire {?quantity} {weapon} (with its optional elements omitted)" and the longer "fire {weapon} at {target}", which extends it with the required literal "at" in front of slot "{target}". If that literal is dropped, the longer pattern loses that element's credit while the bare one still matches perfectly — so the bare one wins and the slot value the speaker did say is discarded silently. Make the literal optional ("?at") so an otherwise-complete match reaches the same score with or without the word and wins on consumed span. That trade is not free: an optional literal also lowers the score of matches that are already missing something, and stops anchoring the slot behind it, which can then claim adjacent tokens.
